  "how_to_read": "instability 0.0 is the only good answer for the second metric, and it is a property of the instrument rather than a score. An arm can be perfectly stable and wrong \u2014 the always-affirmed baseline is \u2014 so read instability beside the accuracy column and beside assertion_accuracy.json, never alone.",
  "question": "Does an assertion verdict change when only the de-identification convention changes?",
  "templates": [
    {
      "expected_negated": false,
      "name": "numbered_list_leak",
      "target": "hypertension",
      "why": "a negation cue in item 1 must not reach item 2"
    },
    {
      "expected_negated": false,
      "name": "bulleted_problem_list",
      "target": "diabetes",
      "why": "a bulleted denial must not scope into the next bullet"
    },
    {
      "expected_negated": false,
      "name": "header_boundary",
      "target": "Atrial fibrillation",
      "why": "a cue before a section header must not cross it"
    },
    {
      "expected_negated": true,
      "name": "true_negation_survives",
      "target": "pulmonary embolism",
      "why": "a genuine negation must survive every convention too"
    },
    {
      "expected_negated": true,
      "name": "lexical_negation",
      "target": "orthopnea",
      "why": "`denies` carries the negation in the verb; no parse relation marks it"
    },
    {
      "expected_negated": false,
      "name": "placeholder_ends_sentence",
      "target": "infiltrate",
      "why": "a placeholder abutting a period is where sentence splitters disagree"
    },
    {
      "expected_negated": false,
      "name": "negation_two_sentences_back",
      "target": "cerebral atrophy",
      "why": "a cue must not reach two sentences forward, whatever the mask"
    }
  ],
  "why": "a placeholder carries no clinical meaning, so swapping one convention for another cannot change what a note says about a patient. An arm whose verdict moves with the convention is reading formatting, not medicine. Unlike accuracy, this needs no gold: whatever the right answer is, it cannot depend on the mask.",
  "why_not_measurable_on_negex": "every NegEx gold row is a single sentence containing its concept, so no cue can leak across a boundary and both segmenters return one sentence. assertion_accuracy.json therefore reports CTX-A and CTX-B as identical; that tie is the instrument having no power, not a finding about segmentation."
